# Tessera — local configuration. Copy to .env in the backend directory.
#
# Storage. SQLite is the single-machine default; PostgreSQL is what a deployment
# with more than one learner should use, because every learner's profile,
# progress and evidence lives in the same database and must survive it.
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/tessera
# The driver is pinned automatically (postgresql+psycopg2), because requirements
# ship psycopg2-binary and SQLAlchemy 2.1 would otherwise look for psycopg 3.
# Schema changes are migrations, not create_all:
#   python3 -m alembic upgrade head
# DATABASE_URL=
TESSERA_DATA_DIR=data
# ------------------------------------------------------------ deployment
# Set to 1 when real learners use this instance. Nothing about the learning
# changes; it switches on the claims a local demo does not need — a Secure
# session cookie, HSTS, and a preflight that refuses SQLite or a localhost origin.
TESSERA_PRODUCTION=0
# A Secure cookie is required over HTTPS and unusable over plain HTTP. Leave this
# unset to follow TESSERA_PRODUCTION; set 0 only when TLS is terminated in front
# of a process that itself speaks http.
# TESSERA_COOKIE_SECURE=1
# lax (the default), strict, or none for a cross-site embed. `none` without a
# Secure cookie is rejected by every current browser, and the preflight fails on
# it rather than letting learners appear signed out on every request.
TESSERA_COOKIE_SAMESITE=lax
# Serve the compiled frontend from this process, so cookies are first-party and
# CORS never applies. Unset means the API is deployed on its own.
#   npm --workspace=tessera-frontend run build     (in apps/)
# TESSERA_FRONTEND_DIR=../frontend/dist
#
# Before announcing a deployment, run the blocking check:
#   cd backend && python3 -m app.preflight
#   python3 -m app.preflight --json | jq .    (machine-readable)
#
# Browser origins allowed to call the API (comma-separated).
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5197,http://127.0.0.1:5197
# Retention target for review scheduling (0.5 – 0.99). 0.9 is the default
# trade-off between reviewing too often and forgetting.
TESSERA_TARGET_RETENTION=0.9
# Set to 1 when this deployment is commercially operated. Non-commercial
# licences (e.g. CC BY-NC-SA) then become reference-only instead of ingestible.
TESSERA_COMMERCIAL=0
# ------------------------------------------------------- learner profile links
# The two quizzes whose results this profile is built to hold. They are
# configuration, not constants: an unset link is simply not rendered, because a
# link that goes nowhere is worse than no link. Nothing here fetches or scrapes
# either page — the learner takes the quiz and enters what it reported.
# TESSERA_QUIZ_LEARNER_TYPE_URL=https://quiz.icanstudy.com/learner-type
# TESSERA_QUIZ_DIAGNOSTIC_URL=https://quiz.icanstudy.com/learning-diagnostic
#
# ---------------------------------------------------- quests, XP and seasons
# Both caps are product policy, not code. The interface quotes them back to the
# learner, so changing a number changes what the screen says.
#   XP a day can pay. Work past it records a 0-XP entry, not a lost one.
# TESSERA_XP_DAILY_CAP=400
#   Recorded session minutes past which claims return 429 and say nothing was lost.
# TESSERA_MAX_DAILY_MINUTES=120
#   Season length. The identity of a season is derived from the date against a
#   fixed anchor, so two servers agree and creating one twice is a no-op.
# TESSERA_SEASON_WEEKS=12

# The transcribed baseline (the results the project owner supplied) is OFF by
# default. Those scores belong to one person; another learner must not inherit
# them by pressing a button. Turn it on only for a demonstration account.
# TESSERA_DEMO_BASELINE=0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- AI tutor
# The tutor is OFF until a model is configured. With nothing configured the
# interface says so and offers grounded, model-free retrieval instead of a chat
# box that cannot answer. Never commit a real key.
#
# It is NOT tied to OpenAI: any endpoint speaking the OpenAI chat-completions
# format works, and several are free with no card.
#
#   Hugging Face  TESSERA_TUTOR_BASE_URL=https://router.huggingface.co/v1
#                 TESSERA_TUTOR_MODEL=meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct
#                 one token, many open-weight models (intended default)
#
#   Groq          TESSERA_TUTOR_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
#                 TESSERA_TUTOR_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b
#                 free tier; no card
#
#   Google Gemini TESSERA_TUTOR_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
#                 TESSERA_TUTOR_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest
#                 free tier; prompts may be used for training outside the EU/UK
#
#   OpenRouter    TESSERA_TUTOR_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#                 TESSERA_TUTOR_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3:free
#                 only ids ending in :free are free; small daily cap
#
#   Ollama local  TESSERA_TUTOR_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
#                 TESSERA_TUTOR_MODEL=qwen2.5:3b
#                 no account, no key, no quota; needs local RAM
#
#   Ollama Cloud  TESSERA_TUTOR_BASE_URL=https://ollama.com/v1
#                 TESSERA_TUTOR_MODEL=<a model your account can run>
#                 OpenAI-compatible, so it needs no code change -- only the two
#                 variables and a key. NOT verified from this repository: the
#                 build environment has no outbound access to ollama.com, so the
#                 endpoint, the model ids and the account limits are unconfirmed.
#                 Set the key in the environment; never commit it.
#
#   OpenAI        leave TESSERA_TUTOR_BASE_URL unset; the default model is gpt-4o-mini
#                 (OpenAI has no free tier)
#
# A local endpoint (127.0.0.1 / localhost) needs no key at all.

# TESSERA_TUTOR_API_KEY=
# TESSERA_TUTOR_BASE_URL=
# TESSERA_TUTOR_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Where Tessera sits: the company site is the umbrella that links the learning
# systems together. Unset means the header says "A Tamuzi Learning product" and
# links nowhere — never a placeholder.
# VITE_COMPANY_SITE_URL=https://tamuzi.example.com

# Named providers, so an operator sets a name and a key rather than a URL:
#   TESSERA_TUTOR_PROVIDER=huggingface   (default model meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct)
#   TESSERA_TUTOR_PROVIDER=ollama-cloud  (default model nemotron-3-nano:30b)
#   TESSERA_TUTOR_PROVIDER=ollama-local  (no key needed)
# An explicit TESSERA_TUTOR_BASE_URL or TESSERA_TUTOR_MODEL overrides the preset.
TESSERA_TUTOR_PROVIDER=
